'''Capuyaquiran Air Lines''' is the joint [[flag carrier]] of the [[United Capuyaquiran Republic]], [[Narubi]], and the [[Bolodun and Kuvari Islands]]. It is headquartered in [[Maruba City]], the capital of the UCR, and operates from its hub at [[Maruba City International Airport]], with a focus city at [[Ominira International Airport]].

== Ownership ==

Capuyaquiran Air Lines is owned jointly by the governments of the three Capuyaquiran states — the United Capuyaquiran Republic, Narubi, and the Bolodun and Kuvari Islands — each of which holds a 20 percent stake. The remaining shares are listed on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor|Sant Cristòfor Stock Exchange]] under the holding company Capuyaquiran Air Holdings.

